---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
	COOKIES_PATH,
	LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LICENSE_PATH,
	PRIVACY_PATH,
	REFUNDS_PATH,
	SITE_BRAND,
} from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Terms of Use"
	description="Terms of Use for iStockVisual: accounts, plans, fair use, library content, and browser tools."
	heading="Terms of Use"
	lede="These terms govern your use of iStockVisual, including the library, accounts, paid plans, and in-browser tools."
>
	<h2>1. Agreement</h2>
	<p>
		By using {SITE_BRAND} (“the Service”), you agree to these Terms of Use, the
		<a href={LICENSE_PATH}>Content License</a>, the <a href={PRIVACY_PATH}>Privacy Policy</a>, the
		<a href={COOKIES_PATH}>Cookie Policy</a>, and the <a href={REFUNDS_PATH}>Refund Policy</a>. If
		you do not agree, do not use the Service.
	</p>

	<h2>2. The Service</h2>
	<p>
		iStockVisual is a stock-visual library and a set of creative tools. You can browse and download
		library images, search by text or by a query photo, and use browser-based tools to edit, convert,
		vectorize, resize, watermark, or sample colors. We host the site on Cloudflare. Library listings
		and available sizes can change as we add or retire assets.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Accounts</h2>
	<p>
		Some features require an account. We use email and password authentication. You must provide
		accurate information, keep your password confidential, and be responsible for activity on your
		account. You must be old enough to form a binding contract in your place of residence. We may
		suspend or close accounts that are shared, automated, or used to abuse downloads.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Plans and payments</h2>
	<p>
		Free accounts can download 500 and 1K preview sizes. Paid Short-Term passes (1-Day, 7-Day,
		1-Month) and Long-Term plans (6-Month, 12-Month, Lifetime) unlock 2K, 4K, and 8K downloads while
		the plan is active. Prices are shown on the pricing page in US dollars.
	</p>
	<p>
		Plans are sold as one-time charges for a stated period. Lifetime Access is a one-time payment
		for Pro downloads for as long as we operate the library; it does not auto-renew. Term plans end
		on their expiry date and also do not auto-renew unless we clearly offer a renewal and you accept
		it. Refunds are covered by the <a href={REFUNDS_PATH}>Refund Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Fair use</h2>
	<p>
		The first 100 high-resolution (2K / 4K / 8K) downloads each day are unrestricted. After that, a
		fair-use cap of 10 HD downloads per hour applies so the library stays fast for everyone and so
		automated scraping is harder. We may tighten, pause, or restore these limits if we see abuse,
		outages, or unusual load.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
	<p>You agree not to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Scrape, crawl, or bulk-download the library except through ordinary use of the site</li>
		<li>Circumvent paywalls, size limits, watermarks, or rate limits</li>
		<li>Share, sell, or rent your login, or use another person’s account</li>
		<li>Interfere with the Service, other users, or our hosting and storage</li>
		<li>Upload malware or content you do not have the right to use in visual search or other upload features</li>
		<li>Use the Service for unlawful, deceptive, or infringing activity</li>
		<li>Misrepresent Library Content as exclusively yours or resell it as stock in violation of the license</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. Library Content and your files</h2>
	<p>
		Library Content is licensed, not sold. Use of those files is governed by the
		<a href={LICENSE_PATH}>Content License</a>. Attribution is required.
	</p>
	<p>
		Files you process in the in-browser tools stay on your device unless a feature expressly uploads
		them. Visual search query photos are uploaded only to run a match and are retained for a short
		period as described in the Privacy Policy. You keep the rights you already have in your own
		files; we do not claim ownership of them.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Availability and changes</h2>
	<p>
		We aim to keep the Service available, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted access, a particular
		download speed, or that any asset will remain in the library forever. We may modify features,
		plans, or these terms. Material changes will be reflected on this page with an updated date.
		Continued use after a change means you accept the revised terms.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Disclaimers</h2>
	<p>
		The Service and Library Content are provided “as is.” We do not warrant that files are error-free,
		fit for a particular commercial campaign, or free of elements that your project might need extra
		clearance for. Browser tools are provided as a convenience; you are responsible for checking
		outputs before you publish them.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
	<p>
		To the fullest extent permitted by law, iStockVisual and its operators are not liable for
		indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data, or
		goodwill, arising from your use of the Service. Our total liability for any claim relating to the
		Service is limited to the amount you paid us for the plan giving rise to the claim in the 12
		months before the claim, or USD $50 if you have not paid us.
	</p>
	<p>
		Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law, including
		liability for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence where such a limit is
		not allowed.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Termination</h2>
	<p>
		You may stop using the Service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if you breach
		these terms, abuse downloads, or create legal or security risk. After a plan ends or an account
		is closed, HD download access stops. Files you already downloaded remain subject to the Content
		License.
	</p>

	<h2>12. Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
